      "gradingReason": "A numeric answer 4 or 1/2 alone does not distinguish a difference from a ratio or verify the required sequence type."
    },
    {
      "exercise": "276",
      "method": "For positive q, b_n has the sign of b_1. Thus sign(b_(n+1)-b_n)=sign(b_1*(q-1)), since q^(n-1)>0 for every positive integer n.",
      "subtasks": [
        {"label": "a)", "b1": "1", "q": "2", "formula": "b_n=2^(n-1)", "example": ["1", "2", "4", "8", "..."], "derivation": "b_1>0 and q-1>0 make every difference positive.", "monotonicity": "strictly increasing"},
